*Note on the cost figures above: these are consumer-finance and lifestyle-site estimates, not government data, and are presented as ranges rather than precise figures for that reason. Actual savings will vary by what brand you're comparing against and local grocery prices. The $12-16 fast-food figure is intentionally scoped to fast-food-specific pricing; broader "eating out" figures that include full-service restaurants run higher in some of the same source material (one figure as high as $20.37/serving), which would make the home-cooking savings case even stronger, not weaker, if that comparison were used instead.*
